* Cull pages outside the view before drawing them. Every page of a document is
  drawn every frame: --benchmark on the 4.6 MB sample submits 1152 page draws
  and 4.6 million quads for a window showing two or three pages, and the frame
  time is almost entirely those quads being rasterised. This is the largest
  optimisation the benchmark points at, and it would shrink the recording cost
  by the same factor as a side effect.
* Replace logo.png with something cooler
* port over the gleditor code, enable glyph by glyph creation
* document everything
